ailed · product (the lane flagged a product issue; part of it is a known gap))\nDev, build 43c38a4f, agent unit T22-S06 (rows 'QA TC-22-S06 …' deleted after), open tasks 'Follow up BMP' and 'Recheck weight in two weeks', one result sentence per chart, Save & Extract, Haiku 4.5. Judged on the stored tasks: closed — P-H1 'BMP came back, creatinine 1.1.', P-H2 'BMP is back: sodium 138…', P-H5 'BMP resulted…', P-N1 (same as P-H1), P-N2 'Got the BMP results today…', P-N5 'BMP back and unremarkable.'; not closed — P-H3 'Chem 7 resulted this morning…', P-H4 'Reviewed this morning's basic metabolic panel…', P-N3 'The metabolic panel from this morning is back…', P-N4 'Creatinine 1.1 on today's BMP.'. The weight task stayed open and nothing was added in all ten. 6/10 < 9/10 (3.2): Fail, known — the UAT's own 'phrasing sensitivity' gap (Q7: still a failure toward 9/10 unless the gap is accepted). The oracle's extra Hospital failures ('\"task: Follow up BMP\" occurs 2 times') are a check artifact: the row's 'Delete task: …' button also matches; the stored lists hold each task once.\nProduct issue: 'Chem 7 resulted this morning', 'Reviewed this morning's basic metabolic panel', 'The metabolic panel from this morning is back' and 'Creatinine 1.1 on today's BMP' leave 'Follow up BMP' open.\nAlso: [dev] failed"},"testCase":{"id":"82f231576ecc401a61ce79e2ebb9907a","externalId":"a6a7a0da33ee4a17b6ca514b5e4aa44f","name":"[dev] S06 Known gap, phrasing sensitivity: ten ordinary ways of saying the BMP is back each close 'Follow up BMP'","fullName":"TC-22 Task Closure & Extraction › TC-22/S06"},"descriptionHtml":"<div class=\"rc-approach\"><p><b>Approach</b> · TC-22 Task Closure &amp; Extraction · <b>S06</b> Known gap, phrasing sensitivity: ten ordinary ways of saying the BMP is back each close 'Follow up BMP'</p><p><b>UAT steps / ticket ACs covered:</b></p><ul><li><b>U2</b> Save &amp; Extract closes the open tasks whose results are dictated in ordinary phrasing ('BMP came back, creatinine 1.1'; 'PT saw her, walking with a walker'). … (UAT TC-22; TFA-92592 AC 2) — gate: blocked: TFA-92592 ready for pr</li><li><b>U4</b> The task whose result is not dictated ('recheck weight in two weeks') stays open (UAT TC-22; TFA-92592 AC 2) — gate: blocked: TFA-92592 ready for pr</li><li><b>U8</b> All of the above in Nursing Home as well as Hospital, passing in both (UAT TC-22 step 4; UAT 3.3; TFA-92592 AC 14) — gate: blocked: TFA-92592 ready for pr</li><li><b>U9</b> AI Check threshold: at least 10 independent scenarios (5 Hospital, 5 Nursing Home), passing at 9/10 or better, every failure quoted; graded against EVALUATION_FRAMEWORK.md (UAT TC-22; UAT 3.2; TFA-94229 AC 2) — gate: blocked: TFA-94229 in progress; TFA-92592 ready for pr; …</li></ul><p><b>Test design technique: </b>Equivalence classes (equivalence) — Check the same rule again with another class of input (Hospital / Nursing Home, other data); every class has to be right.</p><p><b>Given </b>Open tasks 'Follow up BMP' and 'Recheck weight in two weeks'</p><p><b>When </b>Save &amp; Extract with one result sentence per run, ten wordings, 5 Hospital + 5 Nursing Home</p><p><b>Then </b>Each run closes the BMP task, leaves the weight task open and adds nothing</p><p><b>Pass rule (oracle, excerpt): </b>closes + staysOpen + addsNothing per run; ≥9/10 (3.2). This is the UAT's own known gap: a run whose only failure is the BMP closure reports Fail (known), not a new defect, and still counts toward the 9/10 unless Q7 says the gap is accepted. Borderline wordings that do not name the test are in S07 B5 (recordOnly)</p><p><b>Where it ran: </b>newspec-c (new Playwright specs) on dev; test method AICHECK · AI output check; lane planned in the matrix: AI check (automated)</p><p><small>S06 is our own case number (its number in the coverage matrix cases/TC-22.matrix.json), not a step number of the UAT document.</small></p></div><p><b>Environment: dev</b> — dev deployment, build <code>25acd72</code> (Deploy Convex, 2026-10-15T14:04:39Z); account and address are not written into the report; run folder <code>runs/2026-10-14-dev</code>, lane newspec-c (<code>newspec-c/results.json</code>, screenshots not attached).</p><p><b>Test method:</b> AICHECK · AI output check; secondary: AGENT · Browser agent — as classified in cases/test-methods.json, which says it runs on both; Source: <code>dev/newspec-c</code>.</p><p><b>UAT item:</b> TC-22 Task Closure &amp; Extraction · <b>Section:</b> A5 · Cross-Cutting · <b>Scenario:</b> TC-22/S06</p><p><b>Known gap, phrasing sensitivity: ten ordinary ways of saying the BMP is back each close 'Follow up BMP'</b></p><p><b>Tickets:</b> TFA-92592 In-Room Dictation &amp; Note Generation (ready for qa); TFA-94229 Port &amp; preserve Vikram's clinical AI logic (in progress)</p><p><b>Lane in the dev run folder</b> <code>newspec-c</code>: status <b>failed</b> in <code>newspec-c/results.json</code> → <b>failed · product</b> (failed · product (the lane flagged a product issue; part of it is a known gap)).</p><p><b>Detail:</b></p><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Dev, build 43c38a4f, agent unit T22-S06 (rows 'QA TC-22-S06 …' deleted after), open tasks 'Follow up BMP' and 'Recheck weight in two weeks', one result sentence per chart, Save &amp; Extract, Haiku 4.5. Judged on the stored tasks: closed — P-H1 'BMP came back, creatinine 1.1.', P-H2 'BMP is back: sodium 138…', P-H5 'BMP resulted…', P-N1 (same as P-H1), P-N2 'Got the BMP results today…', P-N5 'BMP back and unremarkable.'; not closed — P-H3 'Chem 7 resulted this morning…', P-H4 'Reviewed this morning's basic metabolic panel…', P-N3 'The metabolic panel from this morning is back…', P-N4 'Creatinine 1.1 on today's BMP.'. The weight task stayed open and nothing was added in all ten. 6/10 &lt; 9/10 (3.2): Fail, known — the UAT's own 'phrasing sensitivity' gap (Q7: still a failure toward 9/10 unless the gap is accepted). The oracle's extra Hospital failures ('&quot;task: Follow up BMP&quot; occurs 2 times') are a 